  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ram Milan Rana vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ... on 21 March, 2024 Author: Manish Kumar Bench: Manish Kumar High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:24905 Court No. - 18 Case :- Writ - A No. - 2356 of 2024 Petitioner :- Ram Milan Rana Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. /Secy. Food Safety And Drug Administ Counsel for Petitioner :- Avinash Tiwari Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Manish Kumar,J. Heard.",
    "facts": "Present petition has been preferred for issuing a direction to the respondents not to treat Special Adverse Entry dated 08.08.2022 as adverse report against the petitioner for the purposes of granting service benefits as per Rule 5 of the U.P. Government Servants (Disposal of Representation against Adverse Annual Confidential Reports and Allied Matters) Rules, 1995 (hereinafter referred Ram Milan Rana vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ... on 21 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/174115904/ 1 to as, the Rules, 1995). Learned Counsel for the petitioner has submitted that the petitioner was initially appointed on the post of Food Inspector (now designated as Food Safety Officer) in the year 2016 and subsequently confirmed on the post. It is further submitted that on 08.08.2022, a Special Adverse Entry has been given to the petitioner for the year 2022-23. Against the entry, he had made a representation on 06.09.2022 before the respondent no. 2-Commissioner, Food Safety and Drug Administration, Sector-C, Aliganj, Lucknow but till date no decision has been taken.",
    "arguments": "On the other hand learned Standing Counsel has submitted that till the Special Adverse Entry passed against the petitioner will not be [LEAKAGE_MASK], he is not entitled for any service benefits."
  },
